Theorem RL-25: pair-eliminable conditions (KnownSafe OR both-paths-safe-AND-no-hazard)

  Preconditions:
    - RL-25 governs pair-eliminability per Annex E §AIMS PRE-Style
      Global RC Motion: "Pair eliminable when: KnownSafe = true OR both
      forward/backward paths safe AND no CFG hazard (path count alignment)."
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - RL-25 consumes the RL-24 matched-pair set and the RL-22/RL-23 KnownSafe
      flag; it is a POST-PIPELINE pass over realized IR.
    - depends-on RL-22/RL-23 (KnownSafe) + RL-24 (matched pairs).

  Soundness property:
    Forall RL-24 matched (Inc, Dec) pair:

      (P1) Eliminability: RL-25 eliminates the pair iff KnownSafe = true OR
           (forward path safe AND backward path safe AND no CFG hazard).

      (P2) Soundness: either the physical RC guarantees the dec cannot free
           (KnownSafe, per RL-22), OR the bidirectional path analysis proves
           the inc and dec are matched on EVERY path with path-count alignment
           (no CFG hazard). A CFG hazard (path-count misalignment) means the
           inc and dec execute different numbers of times on some path, so
           eliminating the pair would leak (more incs than decs) or
           double-free (more decs than incs) — RL-25 keeps the pair.

    RL-25 is the eliminability gate that prevents PRE-style RC motion from
    unbalancing the count across complex control flow.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the rc_counting engine.

    Part (P1/P2) — eliminability grid:
      knownsafe_eliminable -> eliminable (KnownSafe alone)
      both_paths_safe_no_hazard_eliminable -> eliminable (path analysis)
      cfg_hazard_not_eliminable -> NOT eliminable (path-count
                                               mismatch)
      one_path_unsafe_not_eliminable -> NOT eliminable
      Coverage gate: 4 eliminability cases. Negative-direction witness: a CFG
      hazard must block elimination even when both paths are individually safe
      (path-count misalignment risks a leak or double-free) — asserted.

    Engines dispatched:
      rc_counting (PRIMARY —
        section_08::verify_rl25_pair_eliminable_conditions; eliminability
        predicate enumeration + CFG-hazard witness; emits Fail on a wrong
        eliminability verdict)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      case_analysis (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 rc_counting engine discharges RL-25 via the pair-eliminable predicate (KnownSafe OR both-paths-safe-AND-no-CFG-hazard) with a negative-direction witness confirming a CFG hazard blocks elimination despite individually-safe paths (path-count misalignment), gating PRE-style RC motion against count imbalance
